<BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/>
<BRL/></TAB><BRK/></NPR>
<BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Determine safe bearing capacity by ramming zero-slump concrete, in batches of<MET> 0.14 cubic meter</MET><ENG> 5 cubic feet</ENG>, into granular soil stratum by drop 
hammer in accordance with the following formula:</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>L = <HL1>B x W x H x V(<SPS>2/3</SPS>)</HL1></LST><BRK/>
<LST>           K</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>where</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>L = Safe bearing capacity of PIF in metric tons (tons)</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>B = Average number of blows of hammer required to inject<MET> one cubic meter</MET><ENG> one cubic foot</ENG> of concrete in expanded base, during injection 
of the last batch</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>W = Weight of drop hammer in<MET> metric tons</MET><ENG> tons</ENG></LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>H = Height of fall of drop hammer in<MET> meters</MET><ENG> feet</ENG></LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>V = Total volume of concrete in expanded base measured in<MET> cubic meters</MET><ENG> cubic feet</ENG>, and</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<LST>K = [Constant determined from the load test] [_____]</LST><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
[<SPT><TTL>Lump Sum Payment</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Use this paragraph for lump-sum contracts, consult with Contracting Officer's Technical Representative 
(Geotechnical Branch) on applicability of use prior to selection.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
